Third-party components:

The Rust crates built into the program are listed, each with its licence, in THIRD-PARTY.md
(generated by tools/check_rules.py). Anything else adopted (fonts, other assets) is recorded
here with its attribution when it is added.

Roboto, Regular, Bold and Italic, version 2.137 (2017)
  Copyright 2011 Google Inc. All Rights Reserved.
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0).
  The files are in crates/openstage-express-export/fonts, copied from Jason S. Wrench's installed
  fonts, and each one names its licence in its own name table. They are put into every PDF the
  program makes, so that no Windows font is copied into a person's file. Roboto has no Chinese,
  Japanese, Korean or Arabic letters; those fall back to a Windows font.

Microsoft Edge WebView2 Runtime
  Not part of this program and not redistributed. The PDF export asks the copy already on the
  computer (it ships with Windows 11) to print a page. The crates webview2-com and windows that
  talk to it are MIT or Apache-2.0 and are listed in THIRD-PARTY.md.

The window (milestone M5) is drawn with egui and eframe, with AccessKit for screen readers, winit for the
  window and wgpu for the drawing. They and the crates under them are listed in THIRD-PARTY.md, each with its
  licence. self_cell, which one of them uses, is offered under Apache-2.0 and is used under that licence.

Segoe UI, Tahoma and Arial
  Not part of this program and not redistributed. The window reads Segoe UI from the computer's own
  fonts folder when it starts (Tahoma, then Arial, if there is none), and never copies it. Roboto, above,
  is the font used when none of them can be read.

The application icon (assets/icon) was made for this project and supplied by Jason S. Wrench.

The look of the window (the navy bar, the menus, the command search and the colours) is the OpenStage suite's,
  from OpenStage Author's design folder (design/DESIGN-GUIDE.md and design/openstage-ui.css), by the same
  author and under the same licence. No code was copied from it: Express draws its window in Rust.

